<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p style="text-align: center;"><font size="2"><img src="https://qantas--c.ap1.content.force.com/servlet/servlet.ImageServer?id=0159000000FSVkd&amp;oid=00D900000010OOK&amp;lastMod=1521233610000" alt="Logo"></font></p><font size="2"><br><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Ref No: {!Case.CaseNumber}</font></p><font size="2"><br><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Dear {!Case.First_Name__c},</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Thank you for contacting us about your experience in {!Case.Departure_Airport__c} on {!Case.TECH_Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If overbooking use:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I was very concerned to learn that you were downgraded on our flight QF{!Case.Flight_Number__c}. I do understand how disappointing this would have been for you and would like to apologise for the inconvenience caused, on behalf of Qantas.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Where airlines have overbooked flights, they are responsible to accommodate customers by moving to alternative flights to get them to their destination, offer a refund of the difference in fare if they are moved to a lower cabin, or offer a full refund if they decide the no longer wish to travel.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If aircraft downgrade use:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I was very concerned to learn that you were downgraded on our flight QF{!Case.Flight_Number__c}. I do understand how disappointing this would have been for you and would like to apologise for the inconvenience caused, on behalf of Qantas.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Regrettably, your original aircraft developed a mechanical problem and it was necessary to change planes to get you on your way without <span style="color: rgb(112, 110, 107); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">further </span>significant delay. Configurations can vary from service to service and the only alternative aircraft available had less seats in the<i> </i><b><i>-First/Business/Premium Economy-</i></b> Class cabin. I am so sorry that this meant you needed to be moved to {!Case.Cabin_Class__c} Class.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If rebooked due delayed inbound use:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I was very concerned to learn about your delayed flight in to {!Case.Arrival_Airport__c}, and the impact that this had on your connecting flight to {!Case.Arrival_City__c}. I regret the only alternative to get you on your way was in {!Case.Cabin_Class__c} Class and understand how disappointing this would have been.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If no refund add:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">As we issued your ticket, Qantas reassessed any fare difference and processed any applicable refunds. Regrettably, there is no refund available for the downgraded domestic sector as the conditions of the fare you purchased permit travel in lower cabins at nil discount where the higher cabin is not available.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If delayed inbound was other carrier:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">You may however wish to contact <i>-</i><b><i>American Airlines/British Airways/LAN etc-</i></b> directly, or your travel insurer, to see if they are able to provide any compensation in this instance.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If minimal refund add:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I have arranged a refund of the difference in fare between your original ticket purchased and the class flown. A credit of {!Case.Recovery_Value__c} will be made to the original form of payment and this should reflect in your account balance in 7 business days.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If downgrade comp provided add:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I believe our airport staff have already arranged {!Case.Recovery_Value__c} downgrade compensation for you as a gesture of goodwill. This comes with our further apologies for letting you down.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If EMD issued by airport needs to be refunded:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">I can see that our airport staff have arranged a {!Case.Recovery_Value__c} voucher as downgrade compensation. We would be happy to process the payment for you and I have attached a form for you to provide your bank account details. When returning the completed form, please reply to this email to ensure your information is attached to your file for processing.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If downgrade comp not provided add:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If a Frequent Flyer:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">As a gesture of goodwill, I have credited {!Case.Recovery_Quantity__c} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account. You can use the points towards flights, the purchase of food and wine through Qantas Wine, or a range of products from our online Qantas Store.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><b><i><font size="2">-If not a Frequent Flyer:-</font></i></b></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">As a gesture of goodwill, I would like to arrange a credit of {!Case.Recovery_Quantity__c} Qantas Points to you. You can use the points towards flights, the purchase of food and wine through Qantas Wine, or a range of products from our online Qantas Store.</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Please advise us of your Frequent Flyer number by replying to this email, so we can credit points to your account. If you are not already a member, you can join free of charge via our website using the following&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/frequent-flyer/discover-and-join/join-now.html/code/FAMILYFREE">link</a></font></p><p style=""><font size="2"><br></font></p><p style=""><font size="2">Your comments about the way this was handled have been forwarded to our Airport Management for review of our <i>-disruption/downgrade-­­­</i> handling procedures, so we appreciate you providing your first-hand experience. I hope we have the opportunity to welcome you aboard Qantas again soon.</font></p><font size="2"><br><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Kind regards</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">{!User.FirstName}</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2">Qantas Customer Care</font></p><font size="2"><br></font><p style=""><font size="2"><img src="https://qantas--c.ap1.content.force.com/servlet/servlet.ImageServer?id=0159000000FSVke&amp;oid=00D900000010OOK&amp;lastMod=1521233610000" alt="Qantas_Logo"></font></p><div style=""><font size="2"><br></font></div><font size="2"><br></font><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="color: white; font-family: arial, sans-serif;"><font size="2">{!Case.Thread_Token}</font></span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><font size="2">Qantas Airways Limited, ABN 16 009 661 901</font></p><p style="text-align: center;"><font size="2">10 Bourke Road Mascot NSW 2020 Australia&nbsp;</font></p><p style="text-align: center;"><br></p><p style="font-size: 12pt; text-align: center;"><span style="text-align: left; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;">***************************** PLEASE CONSIDER OUR ENVIRONMENT BEFORE PRINTING *****************************&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif" size="1" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="text-align: left;">*********************************************** Confidentiality and Privilege Notice **********************************************&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></font></p><p><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;">This e-mail is intended only to be read or used by the addressee. It is confidential and may contain legally privileged information. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone, and you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply e-mail. Confidentiality and legal privilege are not waived or lost by</span><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;">reason of mistaken delivery to you. Qantas Airways Limited ABN 16 009 661 901&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: x-small;">***************************************************************************************************************************************</span></p>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>